laurel 2985: the RPM follows bus votes: the stock enable of its clock scaling (rpm_smd_clk_probe): BIMC INT_MAX, each rate clock of trinket_clks at the top vote in both sets, then clk0 2 Enab = 1, sleep set first. New iokit/Kernel/arm/laurel_rpm_scale.h, tested on the host by scripts/laurel/test-rpm-scale.sh. DDR then follows the GPU level and the stock Gold table, never below the boot clock. Self-check: the MCCC read rises; GCC reads of snoc, pnoc and bimc in one line. An IMEM word marks the first 30 s after the enable: a boot that finds it does not try. Kill switches rpmscale=0, gpupll=0, gpudcvs=0. Both kernels. docs/laurel_sprout/gpu.md "RPM scaling".

